<http://data.silknow.org/object/6087b0be-98b9-326a-a4db-2bd72c5fdc18/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woven silk portrait of Napoleon III. Black and white silk. With a bust of the Emperor, hatless, in uniform and with an array of orders, rising from sprays of laurel and oak from which hangs a ribbon inscribed 'NAPOLEON III EMPEREUR'. The point where the oak and laurel join is hidden by a shield with a displayed eagle on the mantling of France.\n\nThis patterned area is 20.25 cm x 13.5 cm. Below it on the white ribbed surround is woven 'Carquillat tex. Bruyas del'.\n\nThere is a selvedge at the right edge only, suggesting that two or more pictures were woven in the width of the material."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6087b0be-98b9-326a-a4db-2bd72c5fdc18> .

